\f0\fs26 \cf0 FreeBayes\
\
haplotype-based variant caller that aligns the sequencing reads in free clusters prior to mapping to the reference genome\
\

\f1\b install
\f0\b0 \
$ conda install -c bioconda freebayes\
\

\f1\b run
\f0\b0 \
\
simple variant caller:\
	$ freebayes -f ref.fa aln.bam > var.vf			the output is a vcf file that can be used for further analysis\
\
using arguments:\
	$ freebayes				\
		-f ref.fa				the reference genome t o be used for mapping\
		-C N					minimum number fo reads to support a variant\
		-r chrN				restrict analysis to a chromosome\
		-r chrN:start-end		region restriction\
		-g 200				discard regions above 200-fold coverages\
		-p 2					ploidy assumed to be 2\
		--min-alternate-count N		the minimal read support\
		--min-alternate-fraction M		the minimal VAF in the sample to be used \
		--min-mapping-quality N\
		--min-base-quality N\
		--min-supporting-mapping-quality 	N\
		--min-supporting-base-quality N\
			\
\
for multithreaded operation, use:\
	$ freebayes-parallel <(fasta_generate_regions.py) N  	..use N cores\
		...other options to follow after that}